# Security rules — PRIORITY (PRD §18)

Security is a first-class priority. If a change weakens any rule below, stop and ask.
Read `.agents/skills/security-hardening/SKILL.md`.

## Local file safety
- **Never delete or overwrite original assets.** Never overwrite user files without explicit confirmation.
- Renders go to the project `renders/` folder only.
- Use **safe path resolution**: resolve against `FRAMEPILOT_PROJECTS_ROOT`, then verify the resolved real path stays inside the sandbox.

## Path traversal prevention
- Reject `..`, absolute-path escapes, and symlink escapes before any read/write.
- Validate and normalize every incoming path (from UI, IPC, AI tools) with the shared safe-path helper. Never trust a raw path string.

## Agent sandbox (PRD §18.2)
- The in-app AI agent **cannot run arbitrary shell commands**, eval code, or spawn processes.
- The agent can ONLY call **registered, schema-validated tools**.
- Tool inputs are schema-validated before use. File operations are sandboxed to the project directory.

## Render job safety
- Every render job has a **timeout** (`FRAMEPILOT_RENDER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`) and supports **cancellation**.
- Long jobs cannot hang the app; failures surface useful logs.

## Electron hardening
- `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`, `sandbox: true`.
- Renderer talks to main ONLY through the **preload bridge** (a minimal, typed, allow-listed API). No `remote` module. Validate all IPC payloads.

## Secrets & artifacts
- Secrets live in **`.env` only**. Never hardcode keys. Never log secrets.
- **Never commit** `.env`, media, proxies, renders, caches, or keys (keep them git-ignored).

## Dependencies
- No new dependency without a license check (`pnpm license:scan`) and a quick supply-chain sanity review.
